<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> The right Freshdesk alternative depends on what is missing from your current setup. Start with Zoho Desk if budget and CRM fit matter most, Help Scout if you want a smaller shared inbox, or Zendesk if you need a broader set of support controls. For ecommerce, compare Gorgias; for CRM-first service, look at HubSpot Service Hub.</p>
<ul class="quick-picks">
<li><strong>Best for a small budget:</strong> <a href="https://www.zoho.com/desk/">Zoho Desk</a>, which has a free edition for up to three users.</li>
<li><strong>Best for a shared inbox:</strong> <a href="https://www.helpscout.com/">Help Scout</a>, whose Free plan includes five users, one inbox and one Docs site.</li>
<li><strong>Best for more support controls:</strong> <a href="https://www.zendesk.com/service/">Zendesk</a>, with separate Support and Suite plans.</li>
</ul>
<p>Freshdesk is still a sensible choice when its ticketing, customer portal, knowledge base and reporting fit your workflow. Before switching, compare the exact plan and the cost of AI sessions, not just the starting seat price. Read our <a href="/freshdesk/">Freshdesk guide</a>, <a href="/freshdesk/review/">Freshdesk review</a> and <a href="/freshdesk/pricing/">pricing breakdown</a> for the product's own trade-offs.</p>

